      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Titanium content can be varied from Ti0.3 through Ti0.5 to Ti0.7 while holding the ratios of the other elements constant.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation kinetics are active during atmospheric wear testing at approximately 500 degrees Celsius.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing titanium content accelerates elevated-temperature oxidation kinetics in the AlCoCrFeNiTi system.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing titanium content causes earlier in situ formation of a spinel oxide tribolayer during high-temperature wear.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing titanium content increases the thickness and continuity of the spinel oxide tribolayer.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous oxide tribolayer acts as a barrier that reduces direct metal-to-metal contact.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide tribolayer is the dominant mechanism responsible for enhanced high-temperature wear resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide tribolayer lowers friction and wear loss.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Ti0.7 coating will have a lower wear rate than the Ti0.5 baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Ti0.7 coating will have a lower coefficient of friction than the Ti0.5 baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed spinel-mediated mechanism should operate under high-temperature oxidizing conditions where spinel formation is thermodynamically favored.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::chunk::000::abstract::5201bb0b99"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The effect may disappear at lower temperatures or in inert atmospheres because oxidation is suppressed.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "In situ XRD can identify the onset and phase identity of time-temperature-dependent oxide formation.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design; falsification_experiment.measurements",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::chunk::000::abstract::5201bb0b99"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantitative relationship between titanium concentration and the protective thickness or uniformity of the tribolayer remains undetermined.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interactions with other minor alloying elements could alter oxidation kinetics.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
